       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>NOTE: After this happens once, the rebuilder is subsequently able to start.</p>\n\n<p>After modifying RebuildDOManager to <b>not</b> swallow the cause of the exception in this case, I got the following additional detail:</p>\n\n<p>Caused by: org.apache.derby.impl.jdbc.EmbedSQLException: Another instance of Derby may have already booted the database /Users/cwilper/fedora/derby/fedora3.<br/>\n        at org.apache.derby.impl.jdbc.SQLExceptionFactory.getSQLException(Unknown Source) <span class=\"error\">&#91;derby-10.7.1.1.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.apache.derby.impl.jdbc.SQLExceptionFactory40.wrapArgsForTransportAcrossDRDA(Unknown Source) <span class=\"error\">&#91;derby-10.7.1.1.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.apache.derby.impl.jdbc.SQLExceptionFactory40.getSQLException(Unknown Source) <span class=\"error\">&#91;derby-10.7.1.1.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        at org.apache.derby.impl.jdbc.Util.generateCsSQLException(Unknown Source) <span class=\"error\">&#91;derby-10.7.1.1.jar:na&#93;</span><br/>\n        ... 27 common frames omitted</p>\n\n<p>But Fedora was definitely stopped at this point. Derby may <b>think</b> another process is currently using the embedded db because it left a lockfile open or something. Perhaps the embedded Derby isn't being shut down properly in the Fedora webapp's context listener?</p>",
     "created": "28/Jun/11 12:07 PM",
